  "reason": "RNA-only PCA singleprofile is much stronger than image-only ResNet singleprofile in both accuracy and F1, so the RNA branch is the most promising direction, but only one RNA encoder has been tested. config_004 changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200 while keeping rna_only and singleprofile, isolating whether a learned RNA representation improves over PCA before adding multiprofile aggregation or multimodal fusion. This is the most efficient next experiment because it reduces uncertainty about representation with a minimal change, and the result will guide whether later multiprofile or multimodal tests should use PCA or a learned encoder."
